0) Prereqs checklist

Before doing anything, make sure:

Your FastAPI agent is running at http://localhost:8787

In a terminal:

uvicorn agent.app.main:app --reload --port 8787


Open this in browser: http://localhost:8787/health → should show ok.

Your extension compiled once:

cd extension
npm run compile

1) Open the project correctly in VS Code

Open VS Code

Click File → Open Folder…

Select the root folder:
D:\Abhishek\Syracuse\UpScale\ai-code-agent

This is important because your .vscode/launch.json expects the extension folder at:
ai-code-agent/extension

2) Run the Extension (Extension Development Host)

In VS Code, on the left sidebar, click the Run and Debug icon

It looks like a ▶️ play button with a bug 🐞

At the top, you should see a dropdown like:
Run AI Code Agent Extension

Click the green Start Debugging ▶️ button

Shortcut: F5

✅ This opens a new VS Code window called:
Extension Development Host
That new window is where you test your extension.

3) Open a Python file in the Extension Host window

Inside the Extension Development Host window:

Click File → Open Folder…

Open the same project folder again:
D:\Abhishek\Syracuse\UpScale\ai-code-agent

Open any .py file (example: sample.py)

If you don’t have one, create a new file sample.py with:

def add(a,b):
    return a+b

4) Select code

Click and drag to highlight a function, like:

def add(a,b):
    return a+b

5) Open the Command Palette (this is what you asked)

The Command Palette is a search bar that runs commands.

How to open it:

✅ Shortcut (Windows):
Ctrl + Shift + P

✅ Menu path:
View → Command Palette…

When it opens, a bar appears at the top center of VS Code.

6) Run your command: “AI: Edit Selection”

Open Command Palette: Ctrl + Shift + P

Type:
AI: Edit Selection

Click it / press Enter

A prompt box will show asking for instruction.

7) Enter instruction

Type:
Add type hints and a docstring. Keep behavior identical.
Press Enter.

Now it calls your FastAPI /edit.